Subject: [PATCH 3/5] winealsa: exclusive-mode audio - period events and hardware formats

Signal the client event when a period is actually free rather than on every
wakeup, and validate exclusive-mode formats against the raw hardware device
instead of the plug layer, so IsFormatSupported reports what the hardware can
really do. Includes diagnostic warnings for the states that previously failed
silently.

---
--- a/dlls/winealsa.drv/alsa.c
+++ b/dlls/winealsa.drv/alsa.c
@@ -764,6 +764,42 @@
     return need_remap ? S_OK : S_FALSE;
 }
 
+/* Channel mapping for a given share mode.
+ *
+ * In EXCLUSIVE mode there is no conversion layer between the application and
+ * the hardware, so Wine must not silently reorder channels either: the
+ * application's channel N is hardware channel N. The positional remap in
+ * map_channels() exists to place Windows speaker positions into ALSA's
+ * canonical surround order (FL FR RL RR FC LFE), which is right when the plug
+ * layer is in the path and wrong when talking to the device directly.
+ *
+ * It also inflates the channel COUNT, which is what makes this load-bearing
+ * rather than merely cosmetic. A 4-channel request carrying dwChannelMask
+ * FL|FR|FC|LFE maps FC to ALSA index 4 and LFE to index 5, so alsa_channels
+ * becomes 6. Measured on a Pioneer DDJ-400, whose four channels are two stereo
+ * pairs that the USB descriptor happens to label FL FR FC LFE:
+ *
+ *     RBW-DIAG device "hw:1,0": chans req 4 mapped 6, hw [4,4] -> S_FALSE
+ *
+ * i.e. every exclusive format was rejected for exceeding a hardware maximum of
+ * 4 channels, on a request for exactly 4 channels. */
+static HRESULT map_channels_for_share(AUDCLNT_SHAREMODE share, EDataFlow flow,
+                                      const WAVEFORMATEX *fmt, int *alsa_channels, int *map)
+{
+    if(share == AUDCLNT_SHAREMODE_EXCLUSIVE){
+        int i;
+
+        for(i = 0; i < fmt->nChannels; ++i)
+            map[i] = i;
+        *alsa_channels = fmt->nChannels;
+
+        TRACE("exclusive mode: %u channels passed through unmapped\n", fmt->nChannels);
+        return S_FALSE;  /* S_FALSE == no remapping required */
+    }
+
+    return map_channels(flow, fmt, alsa_channels, map);
+}
